Terraform AWS EC2 Instance using Data Sources

This project demonstrates how to create an AWS EC2 instance using Terraform by dynamically fetching existing AWS resources such as VPC, Subnet, and AMI using Terraform Data Sources.

The infrastructure is deployed in AWS using reusable and scalable Terraform configuration files.

Project Overview

In this project:

Existing VPC is fetched dynamically
Existing subnet is fetched dynamically
Latest Amazon Linux 2 AMI is fetched automatically
EC2 instance is created inside selected subnet
Infrastructure is managed using Terraform

This project helps avoid hardcoding AWS resource IDs and follows Infrastructure as Code (IaC) best practices.
